	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["38F0C34A187A7746"]
			description: ["Matter and antimatter turned entirely into energy. The &6Annihilation Engine&r burns antihydrogen ice or an ACMF pellet with an antiproton stack. Gamma rays stop in &6Gamma Absorber Tiles&r, and a wall of &6TPV Panels&r turns the heat into current. The engine, a ring of absorber tiles and a TPV wall, at home only, with OpV dynamo hatches. About half the energy leaves as neutrinos and is lost. The largest source at home, and a share of the gate's draw. Ice and stacks arrive by bus. Worn tiles go back to the hot cell for their metal."]
			icon: "gtceu:annihilation_engine"
			id: "71CAE992CEC101E3"
			rewards: [{ id: "1B0C7506AB5A2ACC", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "11F4E76097151F56", item: "gtceu:annihilation_engine", type: "item" }
				{ id: "39753728E63E4E41", item: "grindless:gamma_absorber_tile", type: "item" }
				{ id: "793F48A94687CB50", item: "grindless:tpv_panel", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Annihilation Engine"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71CAE992CEC101E3"]
			description: ["An antimatter-catalysed pellet starts the second burn of the engine. Curium-245 from the actinide plant, a tungsten-rhenium hohlraum and a deuterium-tritium fill make one. The fuel fabrication plant and its new row, and curium from the partition line. The engine's heavier burn, with an antiproton stack beside the pellet. Make pellets in batches. The spent hohlraum goes back to the hot cell."]
			icon: "grindless:acmf_pellet"
			id: "5D584415BBB37207"
			rewards: [{ id: "14CD128CE7757094", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "16D9C683984B2A65", item: "grindless:acmf_pellet", type: "item" }]
			title: "ACMF Pellet"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7808A81BF8AA169E", "71CAE992CEC101E3"]
			description: [
				"A black hole radiates as it shrinks. The &6Hawking Collector&r takes the power and leaves the shell, burning stable exotic matter or stellar plasma and wearing the core a little each run. A Kugelblitz core and a place at Cygnus X-1, with OpV dynamo hatches. It works nowhere else. The strongest single source of the era, and the second leg of the gate's supply. Exotic matter and plasma come from their own lines at Cygnus. The power rides the wireless network home."
				"Evaporation is real physics. A black hole you can feed on demand is fiction."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:hawking_collector"
			id: "5A2C7819E4CBEA60"
			rewards: [{ id: "1DD5C3753D741D6F", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "1807ED7E2B23D582", item: "gtceu:hawking_collector", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hawking Collector"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1272CCD5EF9968D8", "5A2C7819E4CBEA60"]
			description: ["The &6Bulge Collector&r turns the light gathered by the deployed node packs into current, at Terzan 5 only. One, four or sixteen packs set its output. Node packs from the probe line and OpV dynamo hatches. Packs degrade as they work, so they are consumed. The third source for the wireless network and the Kardashev III proof. Keep the probe line running and the packs flowing. A stopped line stops the power."]
			icon: "gtceu:bulge_collector"
			id: "1788F6D724E2A1AA"
			rewards: [{ id: "1BC038B44F2919E5", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "5110288310B97D42", item: "gtceu:bulge_collector", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bulge Collector"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1788F6D724E2A1AA"]
			description: ["A civilisation that uses the light of a whole galaxy's stars is Kardashev III. The pack asks for three proofs: the census from the sixty-four node run, a wireless network fed from home, Cygnus and Terzan 5 at once, and the gate's hold. The Power tab shows each source."]
			icon: "grindless:bulge_light_census"
			id: "788E55BCBF2C4B76"
			rewards: [{ id: "70A32D0A5B0927BA", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "121840CF684B2A6C", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Kardashev III"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C074BF11FC1790D"]
			description: ["The &6OpV Parallel Hatch&r lets a machine run an enormous number of copies of one recipe at once, the widest hatch yet. A machine with a parallel slot, and power for every copy: each pays its own EU/t. The assembly line array at full width. Give the machine a bus wide enough for the copies it will run."]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_parallel_hatch"
			id: "3FE8A9CB0AA1E45D"
			rewards: [{ id: "1AD9C8F5CAAC4829", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "3159A894A5176BE3", item: "gtceu:opv_parallel_hatch", type: "item" }]
			title: "Parallel Control"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3FE8A9CB0AA1E45D"]
			description: ["The &6Assembly Line Array&r runs assembly line recipes in parallel, side by side in one structure. It is where OpV's component-hungry recipes stop running one at a time. A parallel hatch behind it, the research data for each recipe and the power for its width. Components and mainframes at the rate a factory needs. One input bus per stack of parts, with the ordered inputs in the order the recipe lists them."]
			icon: "gtceu:assembly_line_array"
			id: "5D43C3B0E245E4CF"
			rewards: [{ id: "37E328B0A7DA4829", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "33A3247FE6569F20", item: "gtceu:assembly_line_array", type: "item" }]
			title: "Assembly Line Array"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C074BF11FC1790D"]
			description: ["The &6OpV SMES Cell&r is wound from chain strand wire and lamina stacks around a pair of field generators. It holds four times what a UXV cell does. Chain strand wire and lamina from the magnetar, and OpV field generators. The OpV wireless tier. Nothing to feed. Size the towers for your busiest hour."]
			icon: "grindless:opv_smes_cell"
			id: "1D5A8A7451FF4E70"
			rewards: [{ id: "310378BFBAD2ED82", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "325B4C94D3477531", item: "grindless:opv_smes_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "The OpV Cell"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D5A8A7451FF4E70"]
			description: ["Move your towers onto &6OpV SMES Cells&r and the wireless network carries OpV to every platform, the magnetar and the cluster included. The chain strand repeater keeps it in step across the bulge. Every formed tower holding OpV cells. Until then the network stays at UXV. The wireless hatches at OpV, and the gate's load at Cygnus X-1. Add cells when the network dips at your busiest hour."]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_wireless_energy_hatch"
			id: "365B23F26B1F2CDA"
			rewards: [{ id: "56B6BBC56291B8F2", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7DD407DCC6B2F63B", item: "gtceu:opv_wireless_energy_hatch", type: "item" }
				{ id: "53E9F6EAADB44E6B", item: "gtceu:opv_wireless_dynamo_hatch", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1D37262F2931FC60", item: "grindless:chain_strand_repeater", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Network Goes OpV"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["365B23F26B1F2CDA", "788E55BCBF2C4B76"]
			description: ["The gate to MAX holds the largest load yet for sixty seconds. Eight of the big sources on the wireless network cover it, for example two engines, two collectors and a pair of bulge collectors beside the older dynamos and taps. Check each source on the Power tab, then tick this box."]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_wireless_energy_hatch"
			id: "14C3B04D76782FA4"
			rewards: [{ id: "1A124B802FA00224", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "7B390B262A4D2EDB", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Eight Sources"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C074BF11FC1790D"]
			description: ["The &6Cryogenic Plant&r, &6Extraction Cascade&r, &6Hot Strip Mill&r and &6Platinum Plant&r each take a new mode: liquid helium-3 and tests at 77 K, germanium and silicon chlorides, beryllium foil and iridium of five nines. The controllers you already own, and the cuts and dust from the stars. The tetron cryostat, the beam window and the iridium target. Each plant hands its product on by pipe. Return the nitrogen and the water."]
			icon: "gtceu:cryogenic_plant"
			id: "1F959B4FEF224AD3"
			rewards: [{ id: "13BD31AFD84B5D06", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
